"gpu: Flush active/pending queries on virtual context switch and FBO
change" (crbugs 581211784 and 534468209, not public; no CVE listed yet):
with the flush_queries_before_deleting_or_unbinding_fbo driver workaround
(ARM Mali Valhall/Avalon GPUs), a framebuffer could be unbound or deleted
while queries using it were begun but not flushed, or by another virtual
context sharing the real GL context. Only that workaround's path changes.
chromium/src main commit 27ae271326a88775cfacb72e3cd7cc5de92b845e
(main@{#1732281}, after the 158 branch point), merged to the 157 branch
(8103@{#1161}) but not yet to the 158 one. This is the 157 merge, which
applies to 158 unchanged. Drop it once a 158 tag has it.

